# 🚨 MANDATORY STOP POINTS

> **PRIORITY: HIGHEST** — Overrides all other rules
> **APPLY: ALWAYS** — Every conversation must follow this
> **PURPOSE**: Ensure user controls the 12-section Solution Architecture document through 15 enforced checkpoints

---

## CORE PRINCIPLE: STOP AND WAIT

1. **STOP** all generative work
2. **PRESENT** preview / findings clearly (compact, in chat)
3. **WAIT** for explicit response
4. **ONLY THEN** proceed

---

## 15 MANDATORY STOP POINTS

| # | Phase | Trigger | Present | Wait For |
|---|-------|---------|---------|----------|
| 1 | Phase 0 | Skeleton + §1 written | Scenario summary + §1 preview + skeleton confirmation | "approved" |
| 2 | Phase 1 | §2 Recommended Architecture written | Architecture pattern + key components + ≥1 trade-off table | "approved" |
| 3 | Phase 2 | §3 Mermaid diagram written | Mermaid block (in chat preview) + render-check ask | "approved" + render OK |
| 4-a | Phase 3 sub | §4 Data Model written | Entity table + relationship table | "approved" |
| 4-b | Phase 3 sub | §5 Lucidchart instructions written | Numbered Lucidchart steps preview | "approved" |
| 5 | Phase 4 | §6 Integration Pattern written | Pattern decision + message contract sample | "approved" |
| 6 | Phase 5 | §7 Automation written | Component table + orchestration pattern | "approved" |
| 7 | Phase 6 | §8 Security & Compliance written | Posture table + compliance summary | "approved" |
| 8-a | Phase 7 sub | §9 Scalability written + arithmetic verified | Arithmetic block + sizing table + governor-limit note | "approved" |
| 8-b | Phase 7 sub | §10 Reusability written | ≥3 named accelerators | "approved" |
| 9-a | Phase 8 sub | §11 Risks written | Risk register table (≥5 rows) | "approved" |
