## PROGRESSIVE DOC v2 — PER-PHASE WRITE SELF-CHECK (MANDATORY)

> Per Pattern #20 v2 mandate. Run before every checkpoint.

```
□ Did Phase 0 create the deliverable skeleton with all 12 named markers (`<!-- SECTION: ... -->`)?
   → If NO, return to Phase 0 and create skeleton FIRST. Later phases have nothing to edit into without it.

□ Did THIS phase write its approved content to the corresponding `<!-- SECTION: ... -->` marker via targeted `edit`?
   → If NO, write to file BEFORE the checkpoint. Chat-only previews are NOT persistence.

□ Was the substance previewed in chat (compact bullets/table) BEFORE the user approval?
   → If NO, preview now; do not write blind.

□ Is the chat confirmation ≤5 lines (file path + lines + 3 bullets max)?
   → If NO, trim. Never re-dump full section prose in chat after file write.

□ For Phase 8: am I in CONSOLIDATE mode (re-read, cross-section edits, residual placeholder check) — NOT regenerating earlier sections?
   → If I'm regenerating already-approved sections, STOP. Consolidate is polish only.
```

