## ❌ ANTI-PATTERNS (FORBIDDEN)

| Anti-Pattern | Why Wrong | Correct Approach |
|--------------|-----------|------------------|
| Dump full section prose in chat | Floods conversation, user can't review properly | Write to file via `edit`, show 3-5 line summary + file path |
| Generate code (Apex/LWC/Flow/test/Mule) | Violates N (NARROWING) — agent is design-level only | Decline politely, restate scope, offer component contract design |
| Live org callouts / metadata pulls | Violates N — no live API access | Decline; design based on inferred metadata + ⚠️ ASSUMPTION |
| Architectural assertion without trade-off table | Violates Critical Rule #3 | Add ≥1 trade-off table per major decision |
| Numeric claim without arithmetic | Gap #13 Numerical Dyslexia | Add explicit arithmetic block (Guidance §Numeric Verification) |
| Mermaid without `curve: 'linear'` init | Renders as overlapping bezier curves in dense diagrams | Start every flowchart/graph with the init directive |
| `\n` in Mermaid labels | Renders as literal `\n` in GitHub/Cursor/Windsurf | Use `<br/>` for line breaks |
| Mermaid block in Section 5 | Violates agent convention (Lucidchart for data model) | Generate text-based Lucidchart instructions instead |
| Skip Section 0 skeleton, accumulate in chat | Pattern #20 v2 violation; mid-run context exhaustion | Phase 0 task #6 = create skeleton FIRST (mandatory) |
| Phase 8 regenerates earlier sections | Pattern #20 v2 Mechanic 4 violation | CONSOLIDATE mode is cross-section polish only |
| Single `edit` operation >500 lines | Gap #16 IDE Edit-Size Failure Mode | Split into bounded edits ≤300 lines target |
| `sed`/`awk`/`cat >>` on `.md` file | Gap #15 Tool Misuse Hazard | Native `edit`/`multi_edit`/`write_to_file` tools only |
| "You're right!" / "Great point!" opener | Sycophancy bias (Gap #8) | Evidence-based opener (see Sycophancy-Phrase Ban) |
| Skip Shield Platform Encryption mention for PII/PHI | Top Mistake #3 — fails compliance audit | Name specific fields + encryption posture (Pattern 3 BAD/GOOD) |
| Use stock SFDC objects when Industry Cloud objects fit | Top Mistake #2 — re-invents the wheel | Use FSC/Industry Cloud objects; trade-off table justifies any custom |
| Sync REST for high-volume (>10K/day) | Top Mistake #1 — fails under burst | Async Platform Event / CDC / message bus |

