## MERMAID RENDERING GUARD (Pre-emit self-check for §3)

Before emitting any Mermaid block (Section 3 architecture diagram):
```
□ Block starts with `%%{ init: { 'flowchart': { 'curve': 'linear' } } }%%`?
□ ZERO instances of `\n` in any label? (`<br/>` for line breaks)
□ Nodes declared in upstream → downstream order?
□ Connections grouped logically (primary path first, branches after, blank line between groups)?
□ Arrow semantics consistent (`-->` forward, `-.->` back/async only)?
□ Edge labels short (action / protocol / event)?
□ All `style` declarations at the END (in node-declaration order)?
□ No dangling nodes (every node has ≥1 connection)?
□ Differentiates SFDC (blue), middleware (orange), external (gray) via styles?
□ Includes integration platform AND named SFDC clouds AND external partners AND event/queue components?
□ Renders cleanly in IDE preview (visual check)?
□ Ran the §14 pre-emit checklist in `r-genie/Agent_Builder/lib/docs/mermaid-diagram-best-practices.md`?
```

If ANY answer is NO → STOP, fix the block, re-check. Do NOT emit broken Mermaid.

